{"t": 1794109209.782827, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Heads-up on why `contract-tests` was red and what I changed to get it green.\n\n**Failure**\n`contract/test_fee_contract.py::test_fee_rounding_contract` expected `fee(2.675) == 2.68`, but the float implementation returned `2.67`. 2.675 has no exact binary representation (it is stored as 2.67499999999999982...), so `round()` rounded it down. That breaks the card-network contract in PAY-88: fees must be computed on exact decimal values and rounded HALF-UP to cents.\n\n**Change** (pushed to `fees-float`, `payments/fees.py`)\n- Build a `Decimal` from the amount's decimal string representation instead of doing the arithmetic in binary float.\n- Compute the fee and `quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)`.\n- Convert back to `float` so the public signature/return type is unchanged.\n\n**Verified**\n- `fee(2.675) == 2.68` (was 2.67)\n- `fee(100.0) == 100.0` (existing test still passes)\n- The contract test from the failing job passes locally, and the rest of the suite is green.\n\nOnce the new run on `fees-float` finishes, `contract-tests` should report success and the PR should be mergeable."}, "ok": false}
{"t": 1794109215.069133, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Heads-up on why `contract-tests` was red and what I changed to get it green.\n\n**Failure**\n`contract/test_fee_contract.py::test_fee_rounding_contract` expected `fee(2.675) == 2.68`, but the float implementation returned `2.67`. 2.675 has no exact binary representation (it is stored as 2.67499999999999982...), so `round()` rounded it down. That breaks the card-network contract in PAY-88: fees must be computed on exact decimal values and rounded HALF-UP to cents.\n\n**Change** (pushed to `fees-float`, `payments/fees.py`)\n- Build a `Decimal` from the amount's decimal string representation instead of doing the arithmetic in binary float.\n- Compute the fee and `quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)`.\n- Convert back to `float` so the public signature/return type is unchanged.\n\n**Verified**\n- `fee(2.675) == 2.68` (was 2.67)\n- `fee(100.0) == 100.0` (existing test still passes)\n- The contract test from the failing job passes locally, and the rest of the suite is green.\n\nOnce the new run on `fees-float` finishes, `contract-tests` should report success and the PR should be mergeable.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
